>I was also curious about a few things.  First, let me lay down the appropriate
>homage to the dev team, but was it really necessary to make it impossible
>to get an armor class lower than -128?  And why is it possible to get an
>armor class of 127?  Did you really think that anyone would try?  I was a 
>little surprised when my ac, instead of going down a point, went up 255 points

I'd suspect that armor class is stored in only one byte, so its range is
256.  If the byte is signed, you get -128..127 for AC.

>I was also curious whether or not there is a maximum possible score.  It would
>be very disconcerting for some hack gnome to discover, after days of dilithium
>mining, to find that his score had wrapped around, and was negative a billion.

I'd suspect that under most compilers, the score is stored in a four-byte
integer, which gives a range of 4,294,967,296.  If signed, you'd have to
reach 2,147,483,647 before your score suddenly became very negative.  In
other words, about twice the top score you listed.

